From aae98799719ca27725202fd38f6fe3540d6d90fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 02:01:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(motion): the converter from a kernel plan to a toolpath

Add camcraft_motion::kernel_emit: emit_plan and emit_levels turn the
kernel Plan of each level into a Toolpath in the plan's order. The
converter makes no decision of its own: it refuses a step that it cannot
emit by name, never drops a step and never adds a cut. Lateral rapids
only at the clearance height; below the stock top only the moves of a
proved step that starts where the tool stands. A lift is a retract to
the clearance height with its reason in the notes in the links.rs text.
Exact circles become G2/G3 arcs; leads and helices stay chords.

The K4 motion pin now builds the whole plan (with the entry and exit
stage) and converts it with the real converter; its counts stay. A new
pin runs the camcraft-sim verifier on the converted disc and dog-bone
plans. No old planner and no app code calls the converter yet.

Refs #4269

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
